  "limitations": [
    "An original game model inspired by public Ghost Shark photographs; no claim of exact real dimensions or equipment.",
    "Performance and finite payload quantities are configured for Sea Power.",
    "Native BQQ-5C/TB-16B/AN-WLR8 and Mk48 profiles supply the in-game systems. Sprint speed and range are gameplay settings.",
    "Submerged propulsion uses a finite electric battery. The native Diesel main-power category is used only as a quiet shallow-recharge gameplay proxy for the solar array.",
    "The Ghost Shark plugin gates solar recharge on daylight, completed deployment and both leaves clearing the surface. The native data alone do not apply that gate. Mast control and battery gain need live verification at periscope depth and 2 kn or slower.",
    "A full charge is rated for 1,000 km submerged at a continuous 6 knots before the native 25% recharge reserve. The rating assumes standard fuel use, with no recharge. Live endurance testing is pending.",
    "Contact sharing uses native task-force sensor/CMS abstraction; cross-task-force allies, depth gating, underwater GHz propagation and per-unit RF burst timing/power are not implemented.",
    "ESM and periscope use a low fixed mast with native sensor types; underwater visibility and antenna exposure require live tests.",
    "The in-game release point sits beneath the internal payload bay.",
